From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 10:42:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: isp: add an auto framing control on the
 digital zoom

macOS frames the picture on the people in it (Center Stage) in the host,
from the firmware's face boxes, by moving the firmware's zoom inside the
wide view. Do the same in the driver, so that any application gets it
from one control and no daemon has to run.

With digital_zoom set there is now a driver-private boolean control,
Auto Framing, off by default as Center Stage is on macOS. On, every
returned metadata buffer steps a small integer framing loop
(isp-framing.c) with the frame's face box: the zoom and the view centre
move toward a view that holds the face at a set size, stay still inside
a dead zone, start moving only past a wider threshold and stop inside a
narrower one, change by a capped amount per frame, and go back out to
the unzoomed view after a while without a face. The zoom is applied from
the existing work item; the view centre is computed but not applied yet,
as the pan command is not known.

Where the T8132 firmware puts the face boxes in the metadata is not known
either, so no box is reported yet and the loop holds the unzoomed view.
KUnit cases cover the dead zone, the slew limit, convergence without
overshoot, no oscillation on a jittering box, and the return after a
lost face.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit 62f7ec9fe6ff1ccc6fb5bc79b7af4a40213b2546)
